  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nHere's the problematic scenario:\n```html\n<div popover=\"hint\"></div>\n<script>\nconst popover = document.querySelector(\"div\");\npopover.showPopover();\npopover.setAttribute(\"popover\",\"auto\");\n</script>\n```\n\nWhen the popover is shown, its [opened in popover mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#opened-in-popover-mode) is set to \"hint\".\nUpon changing the popover attribute:\n1. The [popover attribute change steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#the-popover-attribute:concept-element-attributes-change-ext) say to run the hide popover algorithm.\n2. The [hide popover steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-popover-algorithm) eventually say `If element's popover attribute is in the auto state or the hint state, then: Run hide all popovers until given element` (step 7.1).\n3. The [hide all popovers until steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-all-popovers-until) eventually say `If document's showing hint popover list contains endpoint: Assert: endpoint's popover attribute is in the hint state` (step 6.1)\n4. That assertion fails because the popover's opened in popover mode is still \"hint\" (so it is in the document's [showing hint popover list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#showing-hint-popover-list)), but its popover attribute has been changed to \"auto\".",
